  "description": "ShadowDusk full Slang front-end: bundles the real slangc compiler for win-x64, linux-x64, osx-x64 and osx-arm64 (Apache-2.0, see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt) so a consumer gets genuine Slang input (import, generics, interfaces) compiled via slangc -target hlsl and handed to ShadowDusk's existing, unchanged, faithful DXC pipeline. Linux needs a GCC 11+ libstdc++ (Ubuntu 22.04 or later); macOS needs macOS 26 or later (the upstream build's own floor). Optional and additive: ShadowDusk.Compiler's own .slang support (an HLSL-compatible subset, no extra package) is untouched.",
